To solve for 'x' using the given system of equations in MATLAB, you can use the `solve()` function with the given equations. Here's the code:

```MATLAB
syms a b c p q r x
eq1 = ap + bq + cr == 28;
eq2 = a + b + c == 10;
eq3 = x == a + 2*b - c/3;
sol = solve([eq1, eq2, eq3], [a, b, c]);

% Extract the values of a, b, and c from the solution
a_val = sol.a;
b_val = sol.b;
c_val = sol.c;

% Calculate the value of x using the formula x = a + 2b - c/3
