Here's an example of how you can create a web page that displays an image with a caption underneath it using HTML and CSS. Additionally, I've made the image a hyperlink to another web page.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
  <head>
    <title>Image with Caption</title>
    <style>
      #img-container {
        text-align: center;
      }
      #img-container img {
        max-width: 100%;
        height: auto;
      }
      #img-container p {
        margin: 0;
        font-style: italic;
      }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <div id="img-container">
      <a href="http://www.example.com"><img src="image.jpg" alt="Image"></a>
      <p>Caption goes here</p>
    </div>
  </body>
</html>
```

In this example, we have an `<img>` tag with a source (`src`) attribute set to the path of the image file and an `alt` attribute set to a descriptive alternative text for the image. We also have a `<p>` tag with some text that will serve as the caption for the image.

The `<div>` tag with an `id` of `img-container` is used to style the image and caption. The `text-align` property is set to `center` to align the image and caption in the center of the page. The `max-width` property is set to `100%` to ensure that the image does not exceed the width of the container, and the `height` property is set to `auto` to maintain the aspect ratio of the image.

Finally, the `<a>` tag is used to create a hyperlink to another web page. The `href` attribute is set to the URL of the destination page. When the user clicks on the image, they will be redirected to the specified URL.

