  "ok": true,
  "message": {
    "id": "1234567890",
    "text": "Hello, world!",
    "read": true
  }
}
```
In this example, the message has been read, so the `read` property is set to `true`. If the message had not been read, the `read` property would be set to `false`.

You can also use the `GET /channels/{channel_id}/messages` endpoint to retrieve messages from a channel, and the `read` property will be included in the response for each message. Here is an example of how the response might look:
```json
{
  "ok": true,
  "messages": [
    {
      "id": "1234567890",
      "text": "Hello, world!",
      "read": true
    },
    {
      "id": "2345678901",
      "text": "Hi there!",
      "read": false
    }
  ]
}
```
In this example, the first message has been read, so the `read` property is set to `true`, while the second message has not been read, so the `read` property is set to `false`.

