To retrieve the username from the JWT token in ASP.NET C# WebAPI, you can follow these steps:

1. Install the `Microsoft.IdentityModel.Tokens` package using NuGet.
2. In your controller or service, add the following code to extract the username from the JWT token:
```csharp
using Microsoft.IdentityModel.Tokens;
using System.Security.Claims;
using System.Text;

public string GetUsernameFromJwtToken(string jwtToken)
{
    var tokenHandler = new JwtSecurityTokenHandler();
    var key = Encoding.ASCII.Parse("your_secret_key");
    var token = tokenHandler.ReadJwtToken(jwtToken, new TokenValidationParameters
    {
        IssuerSigningKey = key,
        ValidateIssuer = false,
        ValidateAudience = false,
        ValidateLifetime = true,
        ClockSkew = TimeSpan.Zero
    });

    var usernameClaim = token.Claims.FirstOrDefault(c => c.Type == "username");
    return usernameClaim?.Value;
}
```
Replace `"your_secret_key"` with the secret key used to sign the JWT token.
3. Call the `GetUsernameFromJwtToken` method with the JWT token as a parameter to retrieve the username.

Here's an example of how to use this method in a controller action:
```csharp
[HttpGet]
public IActionResult GetUserInfo(string jwtToken)
{
    var username = GetUsernameFromJwtToken(jwtToken);
    if (username != null)
    {
        // Return user information
        return Ok(new { username = username });
    }
    else
    {
        // Return an error
        return BadRequest("Invalid JWT token");
    }
}
```
